</script>

<ProductFrame>

<section id="top" class="bc-hero">
  <div class="container stack">
    <p class="eyebrow">Litestone · shipped</p>
    <h1>Declare the data once.<br>Everything else follows.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Litestone is a schema-first SQLite layer for Bun. One <code>.lite</code> file says what
      your data is, who may touch it and what happens to it over its life — and the types,
      validators, migrations and access rules are derived from it, not written again in
      five other places.
    </p>
    <div class="cluster" style="gap:.75rem">
      <a class="btn primary raised" href="/start/">Start with a schema</a>
      <a class="btn outlined" href="#access">See the access rules</a>
    </div>
    <nav class="bc-jump" aria-label="On this page">
      <a href="#one-file">One schema</a>
      <a href="#access">Access</a>
      <a href="#tenants">Tenants</a>
      <a href="#life">Lifecycle</a>
      <a href="#operate">Production</a>
      <a href="#speed">Speed</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</section>

<Derived />
